  "derivation": "Nourai's bare 'gabl' stands for Proto-Germanic *gablaz / *gablō 'top of a pitched roof; fork', the o-grade continuation of *gʰebʰ-el- (Watkins: 'Germanic *gablaz, top of a pitched roof'). Its attested reflexes are Gothic gibla 'gable, pinnacle', OHG gibil 'gable' beside gebal 'skull, head', MDu. ghevel, Du. gevel, G. Giebel, and — with the ablaut grade that matters here — Old Norse gafl 'gable end of a house, point of an island'. The 'top/head' semantics that Nourai glosses is exactly the pair Pokorny and Walde-Pokorny record ('Giebel; Kopf'), the gable being the head or vertex of the roof. The root→Germanic arrow is correct.",
