  "derivation": "Gk. χάσμα 'yawning hollow, gulf, chasm' is a neuter -μα noun built on the zero grade of the root, *ǵʰh₂-s-mn̥ (Watkins: 'Suffixed variant form *ghə-smn̥ in Greek khasma'), beside the sk-present χάσκω 'I yawn, gape' (*ǵʰh₂-sḱ-ō) which supplies the present stem of χαίνω. Pokorny lists both on p. 419: 'Gr. χάσκω (ghǝ-skō) \"yawn, gape\" … χάσμα \"gaping mouth\"'. The same root also gives χάος, whence chaos, which is why chasm and chaos are doublets in the family. Nourai's form, language and gloss are all right.",
